{"type":"step-done","workflow":"build","step":"build-challenge","status":"DONE","at":"2026-11-18T06:07:17Z","parentSha":"528dfdad08e69bd81ea0f5153ae2c2cbe6a47ca3","artifacts":["docs/plans/202611/logs/819-build-pre-commit/build-challenge-2.md"],"verdict":"CONCERNS","attempt":1,"failures":3,"round":1,"challengeFindings":[{"severity":"HIGH","location":"scripts/gate/bkit-check-dist.mjs:73","title":"A committer ships a payload in `dist/cli.js` past CI and the release gate by committing a legit copy as `dist/cli.js<TAB>x`; the parser drops everything after the tab, so the twin's hash overwrites the payload's in `expected` and the sizes still match"},{"severity":"HIGH","location":"scripts/gate/bkit-check-dist.mjs:83","title":"A committer ships executable code in `dist/cli.js` past CI and the release gate by adding a `.gitattributes` rule such as `tmp/**/dist/cli.js working-tree-encoding=UTF-7`; `git hash-object` runs that rule on the scratch output, so a source comment `// +AAo-console.log(+ACI-PWNED+ACI-)+ADs-` hashes as the committed file with `console.log(\"PWNED\");` on its own line"},{"severity":"LOW","location":"scripts/gate/bkit-check-dist.mjs:67","title":"A commit that moves `outDir` (or sets `noEmit`) in `tsconfig.json` and drops `dist/` from the index passes the release gate's `Verify dist/ is fresh`, because an empty compile compared with an empty staged `dist/` counts as fresh; the old chain refused it at `chmod +x dist/cli.js`"}]}
